--- a/Docs/Design/MediaBox.md
+++ b/Docs/Design/MediaBox.md
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@ Starting a clip from cold in the Media Framework goes: open the source (async),
   - **Warming:** `Open` primes the clip's Sound (`UGameplayStatics::PrimeSound`), sets the desired player name, `OpenSource`. `OnMediaOpened`: `SetLooping(LoopsWholeVideo)`, seek to Start Time, `Play` silently (no audio started) = **Priming**. Once the video time has moved past Start Time (and one more frame), or after 45 frames: the frame is in (`IsFrameReady`). Nobody waiting: `Pause`, seek back to Start Time = **Settling**, then **Ready** on `OnSeekCompleted` (or after 30 frames). A Media Box already waiting: plays on from there (a cold start, a frame or so in).
   - **Play:** Ready / Paused / Ended (from Start Time) play at once (`Play`, rate, audio started at the video's time); while Opening / Priming / Settling the request is kept and played the moment it can be.
   - **Loops:** whole-video loops are counted when the time goes back (`OnEndReached` ignored while looping); a range seeks to Loop Start 1/120 s before Loop End; a range ending at the video's end seeks back on `OnEndReached`. The Separate Sound is restarted at the loop point.
-  - **Audio components** (`EnsureAudio`): owned by an actor so they tick and activate like any component (the Media Sound Component takes the player's samples in its tick; ownerless it stayed silent): 2D - a per-world hidden `AMediaBoxAudioActor` (transient, not replicated, never on a dedicated server, `Get` spawns on first use); World Audio - the Diegetic Screen's own actor, attached to the screen at `GetScreenCenter` (so a sound's occlusion trace, which ignores its owner, never hits the TV itself). Editor worlds (designer audio) keep them ownerless. Remade when the owner, screen, world or the clip's audio kind changes. `ConfigureAudioSpace`: 2D = UI sound, no spatialization; World = world sound (pauses with the game), spatialized, `AttenuationSettings` asset or `AttenuationOverrides` built from World Audio. Each client/player hears from its own listener, so split screen and multiplayer need nothing more; no audio on a dedicated server.
+  - **Audio components** (`EnsureAudio`): owned by an actor so they tick and activate like any component (the Media Sound Component takes the player's samples in its tick; ownerless it stayed silent): 2D - the Media Box's owning player controller (local, begun play), else a per-world hidden `AMediaBoxAudioActor` (transient, not replicated, never on a dedicated server, `Get` spawns on first use); World Audio - the Diegetic Screen's own actor, attached to the screen at `GetScreenCenter` (so a sound's occlusion trace, which ignores its owner, never hits the TV itself). Editor worlds (designer audio) keep them ownerless. The Media Sound Component ticks while the game is paused (`SetTickableWhenPaused`) - a video in a pause menu was silent otherwise. `MediaBox.Log 1` logs its state as audio starts (playing, active, ticking, volume, owner, 2D, game paused). Remade when the owner, screen, world or the clip's audio kind changes. `ConfigureAudioSpace`: 2D = UI sound, no spatialization; World = world sound (pauses with the game), spatialized, `AttenuationSettings` asset or `AttenuationOverrides` built from World Audio. Each client/player hears from its own listener, so split screen and multiplayer need nothing more; no audio on a dedicated server.
   - **Warm start, embedded audio:** a warm player was opened with no Media Sound Component (made only at the first play), so the player had no audio listener (`bEmbeddedSinkAtOpen` false); `StartAudio` then seeks once to the current time so the player sends its audio to the new listener. Heard on a Diegetic Screen (cold start) but not in a HUD widget (warm start) before this. `MediaBox.Log 1` logs the component made, the resync, and a play with no audio component.
   - **Audio:** Separate Sound restarted at the video's time when it has drifted past Audio Resync Threshold (checked every 0.25 s against a wall clock started with it); pitch follows the rate. Fades out by ramping the volume multiplier, then stops. Volume = box volume (0 when muted) x clip volume x fade.
 - **Leases:** `Acquire(Clip, Owner)` takes the clip's unleased player (a Ready one counts as a **warm start**), else a free one, else the longest-unwanted one not on the wanted list, else a new one (`ColdStarts`). `Release(Player, bRewind, AudioFadeOut)` rewinds it (Settling -> Ready: warm again for the next hover), or pauses it; a failed one is closed. A lease whose owner was garbage collected (`bHasLease` with no valid owner) is taken back each tick.
